# Novium Function Definition Patterns for AI Code Generation

## Basic Function Template

```novium
fn <name>(<param1>: <type1>, <param2>: <type2>) <return_type>:
    <!-- body with proper ownership -->
    return <value>
```

## Ownership-Aware Function

```novium
// Primitives copy automatically
fn add(a: int, b: int) int:
    return a + b  // a and b are copies; both still valid after call

// Complex types move by default
fn process_data(own s: string) void:
    // s has been transferred; cannot use original after call
    print(${s})

// Use & for borrows when you need to keep original
fn process_ref(s: &string) void:
    print(${*s})  // Dereference; original s still valid
```

## Error Handling Pattern

```novium
fn safe_divide(a: int, b: int) optional int:
    if b == 0:
        return none
    return some(a / b)
```

## API Endpoint Pattern

```novium
#[get("/users")]
#[description("List all users")]
#[response(200, {"users": list[string]})]
#[tag("Users")]
fn list_users() string:
    return json_serialize(user_list)
```

## Concurrency Pattern

```novium
async fn main() void:
    let results: list[int] = await_all(
        compute(1),
        compute(2),
        compute(3)
    )
    // All tasks awaited; resources cleaned up
```